  "sourceFindings": [
    "The outer ready/refined/no-pending guard preserves original startup and pending polling without an added preflight capture. A healthy reused texture uses one fresh native authority/footprint capture instead of two inside request; updateSkySurface retains its separate original read.",
    "matches and the original signed phaseDrift < PHASE_POSITION_BUDGET/4 comparison are retained. Invalid authority, discontinuity, scope/DPR or expired phase footprint falls through original poll plus fresh presentation(capture). The existing 250ms timer is unchanged.",
    "The first proposed unconditional true after syncTexture was rejected: changed-texture publication can call the native read-time surface guard after a clock discontinuity and return no current surface. The retained RED asserts true != false.",
    "Final syncTexture reports whether an upload/publication occurred. request preserves the fresh post-publication presentation(capture) decision when true, and only returns directly on the unchanged-texture path. Other existing callers ignore this newly explicit boolean, retaining their behavior.",
    "The joined counterexample models the actual publish -> updateSkySurface -> surface boundary with a controlled publication hook. It is not native DOM/pixel timing evidence. The two-read changed-horizon test uses a simple transport stub; actual native publication also performs its own updateSkySurface read."
  ],
